      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The big thing for me is that I could not find a way to convert floating point numbers - single or double - to and from bytes. Which means the only way to round trip those values is through strings, and for networking or data storage that's inefficient (single (format \"G9\"): pretty sure up to 15 chars, double (format \"G17\"): up to 24 chars).\n\nOf course when crossing machine boundaries and using BitConverter we'd have to make sure to check IsLittleEndian and conditionally reverse byte arrays, but that's fine.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
