  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-12-20T21:43:42.723Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It would be nice if we could get nodes for the methods from the BitConverer class so we could directly convert arrays of bytes to other types like ints and floats. \nI'm building something that reads data in binary format from a text file using the TextAsset.GetBytes node. That returns an array of bytes, and in order to get usable information out of it I need to convert 4-byte chunks of it into int32's. I can do that currently by reading each byte, converting to an int, bitshifting it, and adding to a total sum, but that's extremely inefficient for something that should be basically free. It would be much easier and more efficient if we could use the standard C# functions for doing this.",
